PS5 HDMI: leave FRL properly, SCDC FRL_Rate = 0 on the way back to TMDS (v1.8.4)  [ps5-bazzite-deck]

After a 4K120 (FRL) attempt, hsgodd's LG showed no signal at every mode, 4K60 included, until
it was switched off: the TV still expected an FRL link. A PC's driver tells the sink when it
leaves FRL (SCDC Config_1 0x31, FRL_Rate = 0); ours never did. The first TMDS setup after an
FRL setup now writes it, through the chip's DDC write like the other SCDC writes.
---

--- a/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/ps5/hdmi.c
@@ -709,6 +709,7 @@
 
 static bool vrr_stock_setup(void);
 static bool setup_frl;		/* the running setup is the 4K120 FRL one */
+static bool frl_trained;	/* the TV was told to use FRL (SCDC FRL_Rate) since the last TMDS setup */
 
 static void configVSyncSettingFlava3(void)
 {
@@ -972,6 +973,7 @@
 	i2c_cmd_5_3(0x02);
 	i2c_exec();
 	scrambling = false;
+	frl_trained = true;	/* the chip trains FRL with the TV, which sets its SCDC FRL_Rate */
 }
 
 static void setHdmiBasicVideoConfigFlava3(const struct drm_display_mode *mode,
@@ -1118,6 +1120,21 @@
 		i2c_end_block();
 		i2c_waitclear(0x7a84, 0x01);
 	}
+	if (sink_scdc && frl_trained) {
+		/*
+		 * v1.8.4: back to TMDS after a 4K120 (FRL) setup: tell the TV with SCDC FRL_Rate = 0
+		 * (Config_1, 0x31), as a PC's driver does when it leaves FRL. Without it some LGs
+		 * kept waiting for an FRL link and showed no signal at every mode until they were
+		 * switched off (hsgodd).
+		 */
+		i2c_begin_block();
+		i2c_write(0x7c00, 0x00);
+		i2c_write_data(0x7a80, (u8[]){0xa8, 0x31, 0x00, 0x80}, 4);
+		i2c_end_block();
+		i2c_waitclear(0x7a84, 0x01);
+		frl_trained = false;
+		pr_info("hdmi: FRL off on the TV (SCDC FRL_Rate 0), back to TMDS\n");
+	}
 	i2c_begin_block();
 	if (vic == 97 || hdmi_mode_is_hi_rate(mode) || scrambling) {
 		/* SCDC TMDS_Config: scrambling + 1/40 clock ratio above 340 MHz */
